                    {
                        "sense_id": "9072a3ad-b07c-3ff3-91d0-3faa5cb9aad7",
                        "entry_id": "599d882c-516c-332d-8319-c1375a4aaa3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who or thing that falls between different groups or characteristics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0afd4d4-b608-4e90-950b-e2cf1e8bfbde",
                                "sense_id": "9072a3ad-b07c-3ff3-91d0-3faa5cb9aad7",
                                "text": "More than an outsider he was an in-betweener; caught between two cultures all the while shunning his own."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6402ccdb-c028-45a1-b083-ea841d2a5f36",
                                "sense_id": "9072a3ad-b07c-3ff3-91d0-3faa5cb9aad7",
                                "text": "But having two bikes works well for me—so well that I'm daydreaming about getting a third, an in-betweener, light and strong enough to carry me over mountains with a sleeping bag and tent on the back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82db58ff-7550-43a2-96b8-8f2977881d9f",
                                "sense_id": "9072a3ad-b07c-3ff3-91d0-3faa5cb9aad7",
                                "text": "Now, Barney was what some voices referred to as an “inbetweener.” It met that he was never located in a permanent grade level. Back in those days when a student was found unfit of advancing to a higher level, he was held back for only half of the year and then advanced for the other half."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
